 Those governed sources remain authoritative; this README is implementation
 documentation, not an independent design decision.
 
+## Package organization
+
+The `net.fhirfactory.harmonia.model.core.naming` package contains the principal
+`Topic` and `TopicMask` models, their lifecycle-owned entry values, builders,
+the XML codec, and package-private parsing, validation, version, matching, and
+diagnostic machinery. The three public validation vocabularies are grouped in
+`net.fhirfactory.harmonia.model.core.naming.valuesets`:
+`NamingFailureCategory`, `NamingOperation`, and `NamingFieldKind`.
+
+The accepted contract requires internal constructors, reconstruction hooks,
+and matching machinery to remain package-private while exposing the supported
+models from `naming`. Java subpackages are distinct access-control packages, so
+moving those internals into function-named child packages would require public
+bridges or a wider API than the accepted contract permits. The implementation
+therefore keeps that machinery co-located and uses a separate package only for
+the public validation vocabulary, which has no dependency on the domain model.
+
 Calliope's `Topic` is an immutable ordered path of completed
 `TopicEntry(qualifier, value, optional version)` values. A Topic's identity,
 hash code and natural order use only the case-sensitive ordered qualifier/value
